{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/tries\/trie"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Trie","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Symbol","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Symbol","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Hashable","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keys are sequences of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hashable"},{"type":"text","text":" symbols, stored as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[Symbol]"},{"type":"text","text":": "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Trie<Character>"},{"type":"text","text":" holds words,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Trie<Unicode.Scalar>"},{"type":"text","text":" the same words scalar by scalar, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Trie<UInt8>"},{"type":"text","text":" byte strings. Lookup,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"insertion and removal follow the key down from the root, O("},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"m","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":"·"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"σ"}]},{"type":"text","text":") for a key of "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"m","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" symbols"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and at most "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"σ"}]},{"type":"text","text":" children per vertex. A trie answers the queries a hash set cannot: every key"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with a prefix, whether any key has one, and the longest key that is a prefix of a query."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let words = Trie([\"car\", \"cart\", \"cat\", \"dog\"])","words.contains(\"cat\")                                   \/\/ true","words.elements(withPrefix: \"car\").map { String($0) }    \/\/ [\"car\", \"cart\"]","words.longestPrefix(of: \"carton\").map { String($0) }    \/\/ \"cart\""],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Iteration visits each key before the keys it is a prefix of. When the symbols are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"Comparable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", each vertex keeps its children sorted, so the keys come in lexicographic order;","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"otherwise children come in the order they were first added.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The vertices live in flat arrays with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int32"},{"type":"text","text":" links, so the trie holds fewer than 2³¹ − 1"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertices, and copying it copies a few arrays only when one copy is mutated."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"remoteSource":{"fileName":"Trie.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/GrafluentCollections\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Tries\/Trie.swift#L26"},"roleHeading":"Structure","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Trie"}],"modules":[{"name":"Tries"}],"symbolKind":"struct","role":"symbol","title":"Trie","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Trie"}],"externalID":"s:5Tries4TrieV"},"relationshipsSections":[{"type":"conformsTo","title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/Tries\/s23CustomStringConvertibleP","doc:\/\/Tries\/Se","doc:\/\/Tries\/SE","doc:\/\/Tries\/SQ","doc:\/\/Tries\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/Tries\/s25E